  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Increased capacity of Member States to formulate and implement policies and strategies for creating decent work in rural areas</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The following are the major global deliverables and activities of the ILO in this policy area:
(1) Strengthened knowledge through evidence-based research including diagnostics on employment and decent work in the rural economy for informed policymaking and to provide guidance to constituents.
(2) Capacity development programmes and tools on the promotion of decent jobs in the rural economy, in collaboration with the Turin Centre and other organizations.
(3) Global tripartite meetings on rural economy sectors (including meetings forestry, aquaculture and food and beverages).
(4) Strengthened partnerships with international organizations, including the Food and Agriculture Organization of the United Nations and the International Fund for Agricultural Development, to advance policy coherence for decent work in the rural economy and in sustainable food systems.</narrative>
  </description>
